# HermesClaw Codebase Rules

## Split-Brain Boundary
- OpenClaw (Node.js) handles: channel management, WebSocket gateway, canvas, TypeBox schema validation
- Hermes Agent (Python) handles: planning, memory, tool execution, self-improvement loops
- Do NOT mix concerns across the boundary

## Tool Registry
- TOOLS list in app/skills/definitions.py must be sorted alphabetically by function name
- This preserves provider-side prompt caching and reduces API costs

## Environment Variables
- Never hardcode API keys. Always use os.getenv() with descriptive error messages
- HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_MAX_CONCURRENT=1 must be set to prevent LLM slot starvation

## Agent Identity
- Nova is the only CEO agent. All sub-agents report to Nova
- Sub-agents receive scoped context, not full conversation history
- Identity probes are deflected with standard response

## Email Safety
- All outbound emails pass through MX record verification
- Disposable email domains are blocked
- Daily send cap: 50 emails per client per day
- Business hours only: 7:30-11:30 AM, 6:00-8:00 PM PT

## Security
- Semantic Firewall validates every tool call before execution
- Circuit breakers prevent runaway execution
- Dashboard requires API key auth (X-Dashboard-Secret header)